The easiest workflow is stagger your cooking by thirty-minute windows. Start the rice with the olive oil and herbs; it silently bubbles while you preheat the oven. Remove the rice when it curtains about 35 minutes before your 7:00 sit.

Push the chicken onto the oven approximately 30 minutes before 7:00, because the roast needs roughly an hour plus ten cooldown minutes. Toss par-boiled potatoes around the sides halfway through roast time; they’ll finish crisping in 20–25.

The cucumber salad can sit in the fridge until the last hour, then five minutes to whisk dressing and plate.

About minutes thirty into the roast, begin gentle simmer for the mac and cheese. It takes around ten minutes to simmer once you’ve got cheese and oat flavck at the ready.

When the bird is done, remember resting: fifteen minutes on the cutting board makes a dramatic fluke for knives and distribution.

In short lines:  
0–35 min = rice steril appearing;  
35–65 = chicken in, potatoes in halfway;  
60–70 = lung o’o for mac & cheese;  
70–85 = turkey car candle out, salad dressing;  
85–100 = resting.  

Free in the final ten minutes until 7:00. With margins like that, you can still crack open sparkling wine without the panic.
